{"commits":[{"message":"T-3030: Glessner's stable hoist stone as its 4 ft cantilever, cupola ledges wrapped (#1204)\n\nThe c. 1887 Cornell view sees the hoist stone's west side face from the\nnorthwest: through its solved camera (local offset at the arch's crown\nremoved) the side runs 62 px from wall to nose, which a 4.0 ft projection\ngives (1.75 ft gives 27). Its end face reads 0.75 ft wide and 0.83 ft deep.\nHABS 01 puts the nose where a 3-4 ft projection does; its long dark band\nalong the wall is the stone's cast shadow, not a beam. HABS 15 sees the lit\nsloping underside (about 42 px, a 3.6 ft projection) and the foot about\n10 px lower. So: W 140.75-141.5, foot 26.0 ft, top 28.15 ft, 4.0 ft out,\n0.83 ft nose (new optional `nose_ft`). Both northwest prints run the\ncupola's landing ledges unbroken round its corners; they now wrap\n(`ledge_corners: wrapped`, opt-in, no other building changes).\n\nRebaked glessner_house (archive repacked, K01 baseline re-measured,\nsource-use coverage rebuilt); the three stable-end match records reviewed\nand kept `differs` with what stays open. The cupola's height is split out\nas T-3031 (Cornell and HABS 01 disagree on it). L-glessner-hoist-3030.\n\nCo-authored-by: polecat-steward \u003csteward@polecat.live\u003e\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e","sha":"cdee9c69851f5585249809c05188915c0fd942a6"},{"message":"changelog: fold entry files into changelog.js; re-derive merged counts\n\nFolded and stamped by chicago-4d-changelog-fold.yml after the merge; data/liberties.json and source_use_coverage.md re-derived.","sha":"0296270c8f8ed286f7c64b89676eb78a0da6ce97"}],"files":[{"additions":0,"deletions":0,"filename":"chicago/4d/assets/bakes/stone-occlusion/granite_stone_occlusion_1024.npz","status":"modified"},{"additions":0,"deletions":0,"filename":"chicago/4d/assets/bakes/stone-occlusion/granite_stone_occlusion_2048.npz","status":"modified"},{"additions":7,"deletions":7,"filename":"chicago/4d/assets/m